  "query_preview": "..Chilly to cold morning across southeast Arizona\nwith 230 am temperatures ranging from the upper 20s to the \nupper 40s with the coldest temperatures in the higher valleys \neast and south of Tucson. Water vapor imagery this morning \nshowed short- wave ridge axis off srn CA coast. This will move \nacross the area today, bringing warmer high temperatures along \nwith patches of high clouds passing thru. Today will end a weeks\nworth of roller-coaster highs. For example over the past week \nthe Tucson airport has seen highs of 72, 78, 72, 63, 73, 64 with\nforecast high today of 73. \n\nWednesday: the tail end of the weather system off the west coast\nbreak away and become a closed low across Baja and Sonora MX.\nSky conditions will be partly to mostly cloudy as considerable\nhigh clouds move in.\n\nThanksgiving Day into this weekend: Under high pressure aloft\nhighs will run 4 to 8 degrees above normal.\n\nMonday: November closes out on a slight cooler note.\n\nPattern change during the remainder of next week as ensembles \nshow a wave-train of Pacific trofs moving thru the desert \nsouthwest bringing enhanced chances of above normal\nprecipitation, including high elevation mountain snow.\n\n8-14 day outlooks (Tue Dec 1 to Sun Dec 6)\nTemperature: Leaning above normal (35%)\nPrecipitation: Likely above normal (50%-55%)",
